      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Isolated abdominal aortic dissection (IAAD) is a rare form of aortic dissection involving usually the infrarenal part of the abdominal aorta. A 45-year-old male presented with lumbar pain and claudication. Computed tomography angiography (CTA) revealed an infrarenal IAAD extending to the left external iliac artery (EIA), causing ≥90% narrowing of the lumen. An endovascular approach was decided, with deployment of an aortic stent-graft and two balloon expandable stents in both common iliac arteries (IAs), applying the kissing stents technique. Post-surgical course was uneventful; 12 month follow-up showed excellent vessel patency. Endovascular therapy seems to be a feasible treatment option with promising long-term follow-up results."},
